# Setup & Usage

### Installation
To install the virtual environment with its dependencies, run:
```powershell
setup.ps1
```

If you modify `requirements.in`, update dependencies with:
```bash
pip-compile requirements.in
```
Then install them with:
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

### Rendering Slides
To compile the videos and then slides, use:
```bash
manim-slides render app/slides/main.py Main
```
If your scene contains many sub-mobjects, disable caching:
```bash
manim-slides render app/slides/main.py Main --disable_caching
```

---

### Running the Slideshow
Run the slides interactively with:
```bash
manim-slides --folder ./build/slides TitleCA LifeSlide Formal_Def Elementary_CA_Slide RulesExamples
manim-slides --folder ./build/slides TitleCA LifeSlide Formal_Def_Mai Elementary_CA_Slide RulesExamples
manim-slides --folder ./build/slides Intro TitleSI Boids LifeSlide Formal_Def Elementary_CA_Slide RulesExamples

```

---

### Exporting to HTML
Convert slides and videos into an `.html` file with:
```bash
manim-slides convert SCENE scene.html -ccontrols=true
manim-slides convert Title Intro Formal_Def_Mai Elementary_CA_Slide Rules_90_110 presentation.html -ccontrols=true
```
Omit `-ccontrols=true` if you don’t want the playback controls at the bottom.
